.TH "EPX\-INDEXING" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-indexing \- read and configure search index providers; reindex
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing [flags]
epx indexing [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads and configures the search index providers (e.g. Algolia) and starts and follows reindex jobs.
.PP
Its reads require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them. Its writes require the indexing.search_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx indexing providers"
Read, create, update and delete index providers.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing providers [flags]
epx indexing providers [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads index provider configurations. Search and write keys are only in \fB\-o json\fR; \fBepx indexing providers public\fR shows what a storefront sees and needs no scope.
.PP
Its reads require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them. Its writes require the indexing.search_manage scope.
.SS "epx indexing providers create"
Create an index provider configuration.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing providers create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the configuration of an index provider, whose ID is the provider\(aqs name. The JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR holds provider (ALGOLIA or BATTERY_INCLUDED, required), active, applicationId, indexName, searchKey, writeKey and, for BATTERY_INCLUDED, excludedMixinKeys or includedMixinPaths. Only one provider can be active at a time. Emporix checks the keys of BATTERY_INCLUDED before it stores them: it refuses invalid ones (400 Bad Request, exit 1) and stores nothing when it cannot check them (502 Bad Gateway).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the indexing.search_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing providers create \-\-file algolia.json \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx indexing providers delete"
Delete an index provider configuration.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing providers delete PROVIDER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the configuration of PROVIDER, as \fBepx indexing providers list\fR shows it.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type PROVIDER at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the indexing.search_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx indexing providers get"
Show one provider.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing providers get PROVIDER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads index provider configurations. Search and write keys are only in \fB\-o json\fR; \fBepx indexing providers public\fR shows what a storefront sees and needs no scope.
.PP
Requires the indexing.search_view scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among PROVIDER, ACTIVE, APPLICATION ID, INDEX.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx indexing providers list"
List index providers.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing providers list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads index provider configurations. Search and write keys are only in \fB\-o json\fR; \fBepx indexing providers public\fR shows what a storefront sees and needs no scope.
.PP
Requires the indexing.search_view scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among PROVIDER, ACTIVE, APPLICATION ID, INDEX.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
