.SS "epx indexing providers update"
Replace an index provider configuration.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing providers update PROVIDER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the configuration of PROVIDER, as \fBepx indexing providers list\fR shows it. The reference documents not found (exit 4) for an unknown one, as update creates none; for BATTERY_INCLUDED Emporix checks the write key first, so an invalid configuration is answered 400 before that (the not\-found answer was not checked with a valid key). The JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR holds provider (ALGOLIA or BATTERY_INCLUDED, required), active, applicationId, indexName, searchKey, writeKey and, for BATTERY_INCLUDED, excludedMixinKeys or includedMixinPaths. Only one provider can be active at a time. Emporix checks the keys of BATTERY_INCLUDED before it stores them: it refuses invalid ones (400 Bad Request, exit 1) and stores nothing when it cannot check them (502 Bad Gateway).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the indexing.search_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing providers update ALGOLIA \-\-file algolia.json
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx indexing reindex"
Reindex every product (deprecated by Emporix).
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing reindex [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reindexes every product of the tenant, sending the mode FULL, the only one there is, unless \fB\-\-file\fR gives the body. Emporix has deprecated this endpoint: \fBepx indexing reindex\-jobs create\fR starts a reindex job instead, which its \fB\-\-wait\fR follows. For BATTERY_INCLUDED, Emporix checks the stored keys first (400 Bad Request when they are invalid, 502 when it cannot check them).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the indexing.search_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing reindex \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx indexing reindex\-jobs"
Read and start reindex jobs.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing reindex\-jobs [flags]
epx indexing reindex\-jobs [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads reindex jobs and their progress. Emporix fails when asked for the number of jobs, so list cannot check it: a job that moves between pages while they are read can be shown twice or missed.
.PP
Its reads require the indexing.search_view scope. Its writes require the indexing.search_manage scope.
.SS "epx indexing reindex\-jobs create"
Start a reindex job.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing reindex\-jobs create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Starts a job that indexes every entity of TYPE again; with \fB\-\-rag\fR, it also embeds products for RAG search. TYPE is PRODUCT, ORDER, CUSTOMER or LEGAL\-ENTITY in any case, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows. LEGAL\-ENTITY takes a hyphen, not an underscore. Searches of customers and legal entities, in the Search Service and by the tools of agents, read what a CUSTOMER or LEGAL\-ENTITY job indexes. Emporix answers with the job, or with the job of that type that is IN_PROGRESS already. A job is PENDING while others take its turn, PUBLISHED once every entity was sent to the index and SUCCESS once the index took them all. For BATTERY_INCLUDED, Emporix checks the stored keys before it starts a PRODUCT job (400 Bad Request when they are invalid, 502 when it cannot check them).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
\fB\-\-wait\fR then reads the job again every \fB\-\-poll\-interval\fR, as \fBepx indexing reindex\-jobs get\fR does and with the indexing.search_view scope too, saying on standard error how its status changes, until it ends: then it prints the job and exits 0 if it ended SUCCESS, else 1. When \fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR passes first, it prints the job as last read and exits 1; the job goes on. When a read of the job fails, it prints the job as last read and exits as that read does, e.g. 4 when the job is not found.
.PP
Requires the indexing.search_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-entity\-type <TYPE>\fR
The TYPE of the entities to reindex: PRODUCT, ORDER, CUSTOMER or LEGAL\-ENTITY in any case, or a custom entity type (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-poll\-interval <duration>\fR
How often \fB\-\-wait\fR reads the reindex job, 1s or more (only with \fB\-\-wait\fR). Default: \fB5s\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-rag\fR
Embed products for RAG search too (PRODUCT only).
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait until the reindex job ends, then print it.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-timeout <duration>\fR
How long \fB\-\-wait\fR waits, 1s or more (only with \fB\-\-wait\fR). Default: \fB30m\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing reindex\-jobs create \-\-entity\-type PRODUCT \-\-rag \-\-wait
epx indexing reindex\-jobs create \-\-entity\-type LEGAL\-ENTITY \-\-wait
epx indexing reindex\-jobs create \-\-file reindex.json \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx indexing reindex\-jobs get"
Show one reindex job.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx indexing reindex\-jobs get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads reindex jobs and their progress. Emporix fails when asked for the number of jobs, so list cannot check it: a job that moves between pages while they are read can be shown twice or missed.
.PP
Requires the indexing.search_view scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, ENTITY, STATUS, PROCESSED, EXPECTED, CREATED, MODIFIED, MESSAGE.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx indexing reindex\-jobs list"
